-- Every task is sent and runs (tasks = sent = ran), and both results equal local. Without batching each task has its own
-- request (batches_without_batching = tasks). With batching and streaming exchanges each plan sends one request per worker
-- (batches = workers; workers adds up the workers of each plan, and the set's subquery is a plan of its own), more with
-- flush_per_stage. With persisted exchanges a plan sends one request per worker before each wait for producers and at the end.
case	tasks	sent	ran	workers	batches	batches_without_batching	result_same
aggregation Persisted default	9	9	9	2	5	9	1
aggregation Persisted flush_per_stage	9	9	9	2	5	9	1
aggregation Persisted one_sender	9	9	9	2	5	9	1
aggregation Streaming default	9	9	9	2	2	9	1
aggregation Streaming flush_per_stage	9	9	9	2	5	9	1
aggregation Streaming one_sender	9	9	9	2	2	9	1
join Persisted default	13	13	13	2	5	13	1
join Persisted flush_per_stage	13	13	13	2	7	13	1
join Persisted one_sender	13	13	13	2	5	13	1
join Streaming default	13	13	13	2	2	13	1
join Streaming flush_per_stage	13	13	13	2	7	13	1
join Streaming one_sender	13	13	13	2	2	13	1
set Persisted default	6	6	6	3	4	6	1
set Persisted flush_per_stage	6	6	6	3	4	6	1
set Persisted one_sender	6	6	6	3	4	6	1
set Streaming default	6	6	6	3	3	6	1
set Streaming flush_per_stage	6	6	6	3	4	6	1
set Streaming one_sender	6	6	6	3	3	6	1
